{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Praise YHWH, all nations</b> — therefore he said further: 'Praise,' in my opinion, for the sense of 'all nations' is those who were under David's hand, like 'whether there is a nation and kingdom.' And R. Moses said: for it is a generalization to every nation." "<b>For great is His kindness</b> — the kindness that He does with all, to give them life and sustain them. And he said: <b>and the truth of YHWH is forever</b> — against the nations who do not believe in their vanities, and he sealed with <b>Praise YHWH</b> — so do always."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 117, :notes {0 "The inner quotation 'אם יש גוי וממלכה' (whether there is a nation and kingdom) alludes to a formulaic phrase; rendered literally without resolving the specific reference."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:58.559314848Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}